# E2E in the same session

When you **finish a feature** or **change user-visible or API behavior** in this repo, the task is **not done** until `../ecommerce_e2e` has matching Playwright coverage **added or updated in this same chat session**.

## Applies to

- New flows or capabilities (admin, API, anything the storefront or admin UI exercises)
- Changes to auth, permissions, validation, redirects, errors, or responses the UI depends on
- Refactors that rename routes, controls, or contracts that existing scenarios use

## Skip only when

- No observable behavior change (internal refactor, docs, logging)
- The user explicitly scoped the task without e2e

Say in one line why e2e was skipped.

## Workflow

1. Ship the product change here first.
2. Add or update a scenario under `../ecommerce_e2e/tests/` (folder README, one `test()`, conventions from that repo’s Playwright rule).
3. For admin UI, use a desktop context (≥1280px) per e2e rules.
4. Run that folder’s tests when feasible; fix bugs in the **owning** repo—no test-only workarounds.
5. Mark the feature complete only after e2e is in place or legitimately skipped.

## Maintenance

Any change that alters what users or tests expect requires updating the affected spec in the same session—do not leave scenarios stale or failing.
